Package: flatcor
Title: Objective Bayes for Linear Regression with Flat Correlations
Version: 2.2.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("D.M.", "Kloppenburg", email = "192165061+dm-k1@users.noreply.github.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Bayes factors and estimation for linear regression with
    objective priors that extend Jeffreys' flat correlation to several
    predictors. With more than one predictor not everything can stay flat,
    so four priors are built side by side. Independent flat partial r gives
    each predictor's partial correlation its own flat prior, not linked to the
    others. The other three are R-squared ~ Beta(a, 1) with a uniform
    direction: joint flat partial r (a = k/2: every correlation matrix of the
    outcome and predictors equally likely, as 'rstanarm' stan_lm() with
    eta = 1, so each coefficient's partial correlation is flat for any number
    of predictors), flat R (a = 1/2) and flat R-squared (a = 1). The default is
    joint flat partial r; the others are
    chosen with prior =. Their validation is at
    <https://github.com/dm-k1/flatcor-simulation-studies>. One 'Stan' model, which samples
    the prior in its own coordinates (R and a direction), gives the
    posterior for estimation and, through bridge sampling ('bridgesampling'),
    the Bayes factor between any two linear models; with 'cmdstanr', bridge
    sampling takes the model's log density from 'BridgeStan'. The model and
    its log density are built once and kept as files, so parallel processes
    reuse them.
